# OAuth and credential hygiene

Access tokens expire in about an hour and refresh automatically while the refresh token is valid. Refresh tokens still die: revoked access, a password change, a long period unused, or an admin session policy. Treat an auth failure as a re-authorise task, not "the MCP is broken".

## On an auth error

1. Read the status of the credential, not its value. If you have a checker, run it: `{{CREDENTIAL_CHECK_COMMAND}}`.
2. Re-authorise the failing item with its documented command or flow (browser consent), signed in as the account that owns the resource.
3. Restart the affected MCP server, make one read-only call to confirm, and report what you renewed in one short line.

