## Tips that save hours

- Request the narrowest scopes that work. A broad scope can be rejected by a workspace session policy within a day, which looks like a token problem but is a scope problem.
- A "needs reauthentication" error straight after minting is a scope or policy fault. Fix the code that requested the scope. Re-minting will not help.
- A permission error on one resource (a site, an account, a property) is an access problem, not an expired token. Check who has access first.

## Do not

- Commit tokens, ADC files, key files or OAuth client JSON.
- Paste secrets into chat, documents or commits.
- Print refresh tokens, client secrets or `.env` values, even when debugging.
- Skip a re-authorise because "it might still work for a bit".
